  "openapi" : "3.0.1",
  "info" : {
    "description" : "Better Metadata - Better Science\n\nThe repo server resolves CEDAR artifact identifiers. An artifact's `@id` is an IRI under this\nserver, and dereferencing that IRI returns the stored artifact, so every path here takes the\nbare identifier that ends the IRI rather than the whole IRI.\n\nIt is read-only, and it is the one artifact read path that checks the workspace's per-artifact\npermissions rather than the caller's role alone. Writes, listings, and validation belong to the\nartifact server.\n",
    "title" : "CEDAR Repo Server API",
    "version" : "2.9.10"
  },
